{"name":"Tiber","hex":"#184343","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tiber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The river that flows through Rome in Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tiber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiber","blocks":[{"text":"The Tiber is the third-longest river in Italy and the longest in Central Italy, rising in the Apennine Mountains in Emilia-Romagna and flowing 406 km (252 mi) through Tuscany, Umbria, and Lazio, where it is joined by the River Aniene, to the Tyrrhenian Sea, between Ostia and Fiumicino. It drains a basin estimated at 17,375 km2 (6,709 sq mi). The river has achieved lasting fame as the main watercourse of the city of Rome, which was founded on its eastern banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/PonteSantAngeloRom.jpg/330px-PonteSantAngeloRom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiber"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Tibre.png/330px-Tibre.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Tibre.png/330px-Tibre.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATibre.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/0_Tibre_-_Pont_Vittorio_Emanuele_II_-_San_Spirito_in_Sassia_-_St-Pierre_%28Vatican%29.jpg/500px-0_Tibre_-_Pont_Vittorio_Emanuele_II_-_San_Spirito_in_Sassia_-_St-Pierre_%28Vatican%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/0_Tibre_-_Pont_Vittorio_Emanuele_II_-_San_Spirito_in_Sassia_-_St-Pierre_%28Vatican%29.jpg/1280px-0_Tibre_-_Pont_Vittorio_Emanuele_II_-_San_Spirito_in_Sassia_-_St-Pierre_%28Vatican%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia